{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c94d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a070b0-22c9-7f91-ad93-24f3d289098d"},"sequence":769,"recorded_at":1780531400001533,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f9c11a89-ee4c-4cfe-aa7e-08a834791d50","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"f9c11a89-ee4c-4cfe-aa7e-08a834791d50","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f9c11a89-ee4c-4cfe-aa7e-08a834791d50"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Round 6 work is ready for review.\n\nWhat changed (working tree only, uncommitted as instructed; `canonicaljson` untouched):\n\n- [manifest.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go): `hasLoneSurrogateEscape` now also detects raw WTF-8 surrogate bytes (`ED A0..BF 80..BF`) inside string literals via a new `isWTF8SurrogateAt` helper, including the byte skipped after a backslash. `decodeStrictObject` ordering is unchanged — encoding arm fires first on WTF-8, still before any canonicalization.\n- [internal_pin_test.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/terminalbackend/internal_pin_test.go): the 10-vector corpus is replaced by a derived sweep (~4100 vectors) over the full surrogate range in both escape positions, plus outside-range representatives and the WTF-8 road.\n- [manifest_test.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3m2mw8/worktree/internal/terminalbackend/manifest_test.go): new `TestDocumentWTF8SurrogateRefused` pins raw `ED A0 80` refusal at all three document entries.\n\nEvidence, all measured in-session: I reproduced the finding first (old corpus green while gate returned false on WTF-8 that canonicaljson refuses). The low-bound mutant now fails the sweep with 1023 failures and the mirrored high-bound mutant with 1024; production was restored byte-identical afterward. `go test ./...` and `go test ./... -cover` both exit 0 (terminalbackend 90.3%), `go vet` and `gofmt` clean. Full evidence is attached as `TASK-260830-1snnef_surrogate-sweep-evidence.md`.\n\nOne note: the reviewer asked whether the agreement test would have caught the WTF-8 split — confirmed it would not have: it passed while the two implementations disagreed, which is exactly the corpus defect the sweep now closes.","reason":null}}
